WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.090
"IT Chapter Two" is one of this year's

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:05.540
most anticipated films and a lot of people

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.270
are excited for the return of the movie's

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:11.031
creepy child-murdering clown, Pennywise.

00:00:11.031 --> 00:00:11.864
(audience cheers)

00:00:11.864 --> 00:00:12.860
Well, ladies and gentlemen,

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:16.960
there is one group of people
who are definitely not excited

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.550
Real clowns, okay?
(audience laughs)

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:22.210
Yes, they say the "IT" movie promotes

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:24.750
negative views of clowns.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.670
So, with us tonight, yeah,
there's always someone,

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:29.750
with us tonight is
someone who wants to speak

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:33.290
on behalf of the outraged clown community.

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:35.080
Please welcome Butterscotch the Clown,

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:36.115
let's get him out here.

00:00:36.115 --> 00:00:37.048
(organ music)
(audience cheering)

00:00:37.048 --> 00:00:39.753
Hello, hello, San Diego!

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.091
Hi Conan.
(giggling)

00:00:44.091 --> 00:00:45.150
All right, well, yeah, yeah,

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:47.030
hello there, Butterscotch.

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:48.960
So, I guess clowns are pretty unhappy

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.350
about how the new It
movie portrays clowns.

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:52.530
You bet we are!

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.970
Pennywise makes clowns
look like creepy monsters,

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:57.850
when most of us clowns are
actually sweet and cuddly.

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:00.232
Like me!
(creepy music)

00:01:00.232 --> 00:01:04.590
(audience laughing)
(giggling creepily)

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:08.160
Okay, yeah, I--
(audience laughing)

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.200
I understand your
frustration, Butterscotch.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.750
So, did you come to Comic-Con®
to protest this movie, It?

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:16.760
Oh no, I'm here all week at Comic-Con®

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:18.910
to spread the message
that clowns are nice.

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:22.140
In fact, I've been driving
this van around all week.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:25.090
Oh, okay, in San Diego?
(audience laughing)

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:27.851
Wait, oh my God, it says,
who wants to eat babies?!

00:01:27.851 --> 00:01:29.180
(laughs) Oops!

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:30.860
Some letters must have fallen off.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:35.012
It says, who wants to 12 seats for babies?

00:01:35.012 --> 00:01:35.845
(audience laughs)

00:01:35.845 --> 00:01:37.292
Wait, well, wait a minute,

00:01:37.292 --> 00:01:38.360
well, why are you giving away baby seats?

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:40.930
Well, giving away slightly used baby seats

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:43.190
that mysteriously ended
up in my possession

00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:45.460
is a great way to connect with families

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:48.427
and let them know I
won't murder their kids.

00:01:48.427 --> 00:01:49.324
(audience laughs)
I mean,

00:01:49.324 --> 00:01:51.595
I won't murder their kids!

00:01:51.595 --> 00:01:52.550
(audience laughs)

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:54.460
I won't murder--

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.501
Who likes birthday parties?!
(giggles)

00:01:56.501 --> 00:01:59.651
(audience cheering)

00:01:59.651 --> 00:02:01.635
I don't know.

00:02:01.635 --> 00:02:03.960
I don't know what this has
to do with the movie It,

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:05.050
but sure, Butterscotch,

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:05.917
I guess we all like birthday parties.

00:02:05.917 --> 00:02:09.040
Ooh, then I got the
birthday clown for you.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.370
Me!
Okay.

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:13.410
You see, I believe every
child's last birthday

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:15.620
deserves to be special!
(audience laughing)

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:18.090
Which is why I let the
birthday boy or girl

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:20.450
spin my wheel of funtivities!

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:21.980
Bring in the fun wheel!
(organ music)

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:23.860
All right, let's get
the fun wheel in here,

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:25.479
ladies and gentlemen, here it is.

00:02:25.479 --> 00:02:26.312
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:29.338
Yes, look at all the fun
we can have together!

00:02:29.338 --> 00:02:30.171
Yess.

00:02:30.171 --> 00:02:31.250
Wait a minute, hold on,

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:34.420
it says Russian roulette.
Yes! (giggling)

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:38.320
Harass the eel, that is very strange.

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:40.010
10 minute slow dance?

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:40.843
Oh, that's a fun one.

00:02:40.843 --> 00:02:42.570
No, no, no, and what's this right here?

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:43.610
It's just a bunch of symbols.

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:45.780
Oh yes, that summons Prince Hogoroth,

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.180
the eater of screams!
(audience laughs)

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.850
Let's hope it doesn't land on that one!

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:51.610
Now spin the fun wheel!

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:53.110
All right, well, I'll
give a shot right here,

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:55.529
I'll give a little spin.
(wheel clicking)

00:02:55.529 --> 00:02:57.950
Round and round the fun wheel goes,

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:00.743
round and round, where it stops, nobody--

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:04.355
Okay, a little confused about this.

00:03:04.355 --> 00:03:06.507
(audience laughs)
Knows, woo-hoo!

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.500
Okay, I'm confused, it
says animal balloons.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:12.870
Yes.
Don't you mean

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:15.427
balloon animals?
Oh, you'll wish I did.

00:03:15.427 --> 00:03:16.840
(audience laughs)

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:18.810
I make all sorts of animal balloons

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:21.470
by finding flat little
fellas near the highway,

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:23.848
then filling them with helium!
(audience laughing)

00:03:23.848 --> 00:03:25.990
(creepy music)
See?

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:28.780
I found this possum near the I-5 on-let.

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:30.090
That's a possum?!

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:31.610
Yes, it used to be.
Oh.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:35.610
And here's a snake I
made into a dog balloon!

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:36.640
Ruff ruff!
(audience laughing)

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:37.473
Hiss hiss!

00:03:37.473 --> 00:03:38.970
Okay, you know what?

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:40.650
I think you've wasted enough of our time.

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.250
Agree to disagree!
All right.

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:43.820
Before I leave, I just want to say

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:45.950
please don't come to
Comic-Con® in Pennywise cosplay

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.770
when there are so many
other fun cosplay ideas

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.460
that don't glamorize
child-murdering clowns.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:52.293
All right.
(audience laughs)

00:03:52.293 --> 00:03:53.410
Here's a great one!

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:54.713
Look familiar, Conan?

00:03:54.713 --> 00:03:56.700
(organ music)
Oh wow, yeah, of course.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:58.090
It's Hello Kitty.
(audience cheering)

00:03:58.090 --> 00:03:59.340
Yes, exactly!

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:03.730
What a cute, sweet idea
for cosplay at Comic-Con®!

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:05.240
And I got all the details right,

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:07.430
she's even anatomically correct.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:10.609
Huh?
(audience laughing)

00:04:10.609 --> 00:04:13.812
(cats mewling)
Drink up, little kitties!

00:04:13.812 --> 00:04:16.220
Drink up, little ones!
(suckling)

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:17.493
That's really, I don't,
no one, no, no one wants--

00:04:17.493 --> 00:04:18.780
Are you thirsty, Conan?

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:19.780
No, I'm not thirsty.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:21.610
And no one wants to see that.
(audience laughing)

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:23.360
Okay.
That's really not good.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:25.230
Here's another great cosplay idea

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:26.870
for fans of science fiction!

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:29.820
Recognize this classic character, Conan?

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:30.780
I'm not sure,

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:32.580
I guess it's just some
kind of astronaut, huh?

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.963
Ooh, well maybe this will jog your memory.

00:04:34.963 --> 00:04:36.299
(screaming)

00:04:36.299 --> 00:04:38.150
(screeching)

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:40.147
(audience laughing)

00:04:40.147 --> 00:04:41.064
Peek-a-boo!

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:44.285
You see, it's the
crotch-burster from Aliens!

00:04:44.285 --> 00:04:46.010
(giggling)

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:48.469
Now, who wants to see
me make him spit acid?!

00:04:48.469 --> 00:04:49.302
(audience cheers)
Now wait a minute,

00:04:49.302 --> 00:04:50.620
wait a minute, no!
C'mon!

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:51.850
No!
I just have to choke him

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:53.161
a little!
No, we don't, no, no, no--

00:04:53.161 --> 00:04:54.547
I just have to choke him
a little bit like this!

00:04:54.547 --> 00:04:57.772
No, no, no!
(audience cheering)

00:04:57.772 --> 00:04:59.358
Spurt the acid!

00:04:59.358 --> 00:05:00.251
No, no, no, get away, get away, get away!

00:05:00.251 --> 00:05:01.351
Spurt the acid!

00:05:01.351 --> 00:05:02.286
No, no!

00:05:02.286 --> 00:05:03.472
Tickle his stomach while I choke him!

00:05:03.472 --> 00:05:04.305
Yeah, no, I'm not going to.
No?

00:05:04.305 --> 00:05:05.710
Butterscotch the Clown, everybody,

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:07.410
we have a lot more show coming up.

